  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1152 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nAn upper trough will deepen across the Great Lakes Region into\nthe Mid Atlantic Thursday through Friday. Northerly flow will \nremain in place on the backside of the trough across the Central \nPlains. Cooler air will be drawn in Thursday into Friday,\nespecially across the east. Highs Thursday will contrast from the \nlow 40s northeast to the upper 50s to low 60s western Sandhills and \nsouthwest areas. Still cool Friday from the mid 40s to low 50s east \nand mid to upper 50s west. A transitory upper ridge will cross the\narea Saturday as a negatively tilted upper trough moves through the \nCentral Rockies. This system will bring a light chance for rain \nlate Saturday into Sunday mainly across the south and east. Highs \nreturn to the 50s Saturday and Sunday with upper height rises and \ndry conditions expected by Monday. Lows 25 to 30 Thursday night and\n30 to 35 Friday night, then mid 30s Saturday night and Sunday night.",
